    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d823">

                <pb facs="0890" n="802" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg802"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Jackson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-07-08"><hi rendition="#italic">July 8,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 10, Servian series.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 44, Servian series, of the 14th ultimo, in regard to the proposed coronation
                    of King Peter of Servia.</p>
                <pb facs="0891" n="803" xml:id="pg803"/>
                <p>In view of your report that it is expected that special representatives will be
                    sent from Russia, Italy, and Montenegro, and that other countries will be
                    represented by their ministers at Belgrade, and that if that should prove to be
                    the case you will arrange to go to Belgrade, taking Mr. Wilson with you, I have
                    to say that your purpose to attend the coronation is approved, if no unforeseen
                    objection appear.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
